<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-1> <https://threadbiz.example/#ownerReason> "Don't say a dish recipe is passed down through generations unless my note says so." .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-1> <https://threadbiz.example/#recordedAt> "2026-09-24T06:20:16.653Z" .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-1> <https://threadbiz.example/#rejectedCaption> "From our very first drop, I wanted to share dishes that felt like coming home. This week, we're making a small batch of vegetable and herb soup, using the last of the season's tomatoes, fresh parsley, and basil. It's a recipe passed down through generations, full of simple goodness. Place your pre-order today." .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-1> <https://threadbiz.example/#rejectedImage> "https://agent.livepeer.org/a/aHR0cHM6Ly83eTRmbHpwdWxndjRjbzZyLnB1YmxpYy5ibG9iLnZlcmNlbC1zdG9yYWdlLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzE3OTAyMzA1MDUyNDktbno3dXR3LmpwZWc.f8b4ab8c0417fec4/1790230505249-nz7utw.jpeg" .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-1> <https://threadbiz.example/#runId> "entry-000-20260924T061434" .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://threadbiz.example/#LessonOccurrence> .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-2> <https://threadbiz.example/#ownerReason> "Don't mention a grandmother or say the recipe has been in the family for generations unless my note says so." .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-2> <https://threadbiz.example/#recordedAt> "2026-09-24T06:31:15.672Z" .
<https://threadbiz.example/#lesson-001-occurrence-2> <https://threadbiz.example/#rejectedCaption> "Our first weekly offering, a hearty vegetable and herb soup, uses up the very last of this season's tomatoes, just like my grandmother used to do. It’s a recipe that’s been in our family for generations, a comforting taste of home. We're so happy to share it with you. Please pre-order for your bowl." .
